.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt LIF 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm lif
.Nd terminal multiplexer with tmux commands and key bindings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 2uvV
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl L Ar socket-name
.Op Fl S Ar socket-path
.Op Ar command Op Ar flags
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs programs in panes inside windows inside sessions, keeps them running
when the terminal goes away, and lets several terminals attach to the same
session.
It implements a large part of
.Xr tmux 1 Ns 's
command language, targets, formats, options and default key bindings.
.Pp
The first
.Nm
command that needs a server starts one in the background on the socket.
The server reads its configuration file once at start-up (see
.Sx FILES ) .
Without a
.Ar command ,
.Nm
runs
.Ic new-session .
Several commands can be given on one command line, separated by a
.Ql \e\&;
argument.
.Pp
By default the prefix key is
.Ql C-b ;
keys pressed after it run the commands of the prefix key table (see
.Sx KEY BINDINGS ) .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-S socket-path"
.It Fl 2 , Fl u
Accepted for tmux compatibility; 256 colors and UTF-8 are always on.
.It Fl f Ar file
Configuration file for a server started by this command.
A relative path is relative to the current directory.
A server that is already running keeps its configuration.
.It Fl h
Print the usage line and exit.
.It Fl L Ar socket-name
Use the socket
.Ar socket-name
in the default socket directory instead of
.Pa default .
.It Fl S Ar socket-path
Use the socket at
.Ar socket-path .
.It Fl v
Make a server started by this command log to
.Pa lif-server- Ns Ar pid Ns Pa .log
in the socket's directory.
.It Fl V
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh FILE COMMANDS
These commands work on configuration files and need no server:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic check-config Op Ar file
Check
.Ar file
(by default the file the server would read) and print each problem as
.Ar file : Ns Ar line : Ns Ar column : Li "error: " Ns Ar message .
Prints nothing for a file without problems.
.It Ic print-config
Print the documented example configuration, in which every value is the
default.
.It Ic migrate-tmux-conf Op Ar file
Translate a
.Xr tmux 1
configuration file (by default
.Pa ~/.tmux.conf )
to
.Nm Ns 's
TOML format on standard output, and print each line that was not
translated, with the reason, on standard error.
.El
.Sh TARGETS
Commands find sessions, windows and panes with
.Fl t
(and
.Fl s
for a source) as in
.Xr tmux 1 :
.Ar session : Ns Ar window . Ns Ar pane ,
where each part may be a name, an index, a unique prefix or a glob, or an id
.Li ($1, @2, %3) .
A leading
.Ql =
asks for an exact name.
Windows can also be
.Li "{start} ^ {end} $ {last} ! {next} + {previous} -"
and
.Li +N , -N ;
panes
.Li "{last} ! {next} + {previous} - {top} {bottom} {left} {right}"
and
.Li {up-of} {down-of} {left-of} {right-of} .
Inside a pane,
.Nm
commands without
.Fl t
act on that pane when they reach the same server.
.Sh FORMATS
Formats are expanded in
.Fl F
arguments,
.Ic display-message ,
window names, working directories and the status line:
.Li #{name} ,
the aliases
.Li #S #I #W #P #T #D #F #H #h ## ,
conditionals
.Li #{?cond,a,b} ,
comparisons
.Li #{==:a,b} ,
and modifiers such as
.Li "#{t:...} #{b:...} #{=N:...}"
(the full list is in
.Pa docs/tmux-migration.md ) .
A name that is not a variable is looked up as an option.
.Li #(command)
expands to nothing.
.Sh COMMANDS
Commands, their aliases and their flags as
.Nm
accepts them.
Flags of the
.Xr tmux 1
command that are not shown are rejected with
.Dq unknown flag .
Any unambiguous prefix of a command name works.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
